  "reason": "With no prior experiments, the most informative first step is to establish a well-balanced multimodal baseline that uses standard, reasonable choices across all design dimensions (multiprofile for data richness, scgpt as a pretrained domain-specific RNA encoder, resnet50 as a standard image encoder, avgpool as a simple robust aggregation, and concat as the simplest fusion). This anchors the search: subsequent experiments can isolate the effect of each component (e.g., swapping to imagenet_vit_l, transformer aggregation, weighted fusion, or comparing to image-only/RNA-only baselines) against this reference. It avoids overcommitting to a complex or unusual configuration while still exercising the full multimodal pipeline, making it the highest-information first experiment under a limited budget."
}

